-- What a triage verdict wrote into the library, so undo takes back exactly that (#902, #790).
-- The filename is the version this migrates FROM: 32.sqm takes a v32 database to v33 (fixture 33.db).
--
-- NUMBERING: claimed on the #902/#790/#791/#792 branch, which opened after 29.sqm (#767) merged to
-- develop. 30.sqm (#853) and 31.sqm (#785) landed while it was open, so it took 32. `verifyMigrations`
-- cannot see a collision, so re-check this number against develop before merging.
--
-- entryAddedAtEpochMs: the `addedAtEpochMs` of the collection entry the verdict created, read right
-- after the add. Undo removes the entry only while its current stamp still equals this one, so an
-- entry the person removed and added again while the undo snackbar was open survives (#902). NULL
-- for every row written before this column, and for any verdict that did not create its entry; a
-- NULL stamp never authorises a removal.
--
-- tickedEpisodeIds: the viewing ids (EpisodeId@watchedAtEpochMs) the verdict itself wrote, comma-separated (an
-- id never contains a comma). Undo removes exactly these viewings and leaves every viewing the person
-- made themselves (#790). Empty for every row written before this column; undo then un-ticks nothing.
ALTER TABLE triageDecision ADD COLUMN entryAddedAtEpochMs INTEGER;
ALTER TABLE triageDecision ADD COLUMN tickedEpisodeIds TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
